117
00:09:29,230 --> 00:09:35,175
[SPEAKER_00]: I instructed Charlie to let you know whether to play back, play in, to the right or left, which I did.

118
00:09:35,476 --> 00:09:36,897
[SPEAKER_00]: And Charlie was a great help to me.

119
00:09:37,137 --> 00:09:41,060
[SPEAKER_00]: Because Charlie had played a few years in the major leagues and was on his way out.

120
00:09:41,621 --> 00:09:43,382
[SPEAKER_00]: And he was great with young ballplayers.

121
00:09:43,983 --> 00:09:46,165
[SPEAKER_00]: And he did help me a great deal in moving me around.

122
00:09:47,338 --> 00:09:51,667
[SPEAKER_01]: I understand 1930 was the year the averages were all the way up though, wasn't it?

123
00:09:52,108 --> 00:09:54,273
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, well I think the truth is that

124
00:09:54,973 --> 00:09:56,674
[SPEAKER_00]: We had a lively ball.

125
00:09:56,974 --> 00:09:57,394
[SPEAKER_00]: I didn't know.

126
00:09:57,414 --> 00:10:09,121
[SPEAKER_00]: That was the first year I was in the big leagues, but they all said that the ball was really, really lively and that even myself, I hit, oh, I don't know, eight or nine, ten home runs or something like that.

127
00:10:10,001 --> 00:10:14,424
[SPEAKER_00]: And I hit some balls that were shots over the left field wall that I didn't believe I could hit a ball that far.

128
00:10:14,984 --> 00:10:16,405
[SPEAKER_00]: So the ball had to be lively.

129
00:10:16,665 --> 00:10:17,925
[SPEAKER_01]: That's when he was with the Cubs.

130
00:10:20,979 --> 00:10:23,161
[SPEAKER_00]: Knocked in, I believe, 190 runs, too.

131
00:10:23,181 --> 00:10:24,222
[SPEAKER_01]: Nobody will ever try that one.

132
00:10:24,322 --> 00:10:25,804
[SPEAKER_00]: No, that's quite a season.

133
00:10:25,884 --> 00:10:29,948
[SPEAKER_00]: I think the Phillies finished way down, and they had a team batting average of over 300.

134
00:10:30,048 --> 00:10:32,050
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, I believe they had a team batting average of 300.

135
00:10:32,070 --> 00:10:34,252
[SPEAKER_00]: But then again, they had a ballpark.

136
00:10:34,272 --> 00:10:35,393
[SPEAKER_00]: It was a hitting paradise.

137
00:10:35,413 --> 00:10:36,354
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you like to hit there?

138
00:10:36,494 --> 00:10:37,395
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yes, yes.

139
00:10:37,455 --> 00:10:40,017
[SPEAKER_00]: That's when I had one of my biggest days in the major leagues.

140
00:10:40,638 --> 00:10:44,161
[SPEAKER_00]: I had six hits on six times of bat for nine innings.

141
00:10:45,877 --> 00:10:46,837
[SPEAKER_01]: Your right hand hitter though.

142
00:10:46,857 --> 00:10:48,398
[SPEAKER_01]: Were you hitting the right field?

143
00:10:48,618 --> 00:10:51,199
[SPEAKER_00]: No, left field wasn't too far.

144
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:55,481
[SPEAKER_00]: At the power alleys about 345, 350 at the most.

145
00:10:55,922 --> 00:10:57,782
[SPEAKER_00]: Right field was only about 275.

146
00:10:58,203 --> 00:11:00,804
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where Chuck Klein hit a lot of his home runs.

147
00:11:00,824 --> 00:11:03,125
[SPEAKER_01]: He went over to Chicago and didn't hit so many home runs.

148
00:11:03,145 --> 00:11:05,126
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it was a little further over than Chicago.

149
00:11:10,815 --> 00:11:13,496
[SPEAKER_01]: Any problems, any pitchers that gave you trouble in this first year?

150
00:11:13,796 --> 00:11:17,277
[SPEAKER_00]: When I first started out, yes, they all gave me problems.

151
00:11:17,317 --> 00:11:19,098
[SPEAKER_00]: But then later on, I got going.

152
00:11:19,118 --> 00:11:19,978
[SPEAKER_00]: I hit them all.

153
00:11:20,359 --> 00:11:23,360
[SPEAKER_00]: I was only hitting about 210 up until June.

154
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:26,181
[SPEAKER_00]: As I said, I finished the season hitting 312.

155
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:29,042
