1018
01:00:28,922 --> 01:00:31,885
[SPEAKER_00]: Then I took myself out of the lineup.

1019
01:00:31,925 --> 01:00:33,246
[SPEAKER_00]: It was tough trying to manage.

1020
01:00:33,586 --> 01:00:36,208
[SPEAKER_00]: That was my first venture as a manager.

1021
01:00:36,228 --> 01:00:42,092
[SPEAKER_00]: I was trying to play and manage.

1022
01:00:42,132 --> 01:00:43,573
[SPEAKER_00]: I had no coaches on the club.

1023
01:00:43,593 --> 01:00:46,495
[SPEAKER_00]: I had to do everything myself, which was a tough job.

1024
01:00:46,776 --> 01:00:51,159
[SPEAKER_00]: Even the small class A clubs now have a coach or two.

1025
01:00:51,652 --> 01:00:54,953
[SPEAKER_00]: Like here Tampa has two of them and they're in class A baseball.

1026
01:00:55,393 --> 01:00:58,534
[SPEAKER_00]: And the manager has a lot of help, but I didn't have it.

1027
01:00:58,574 --> 01:01:02,735
[SPEAKER_00]: I had to pick out one of my older pitchers to help me around with this and that.

1028
01:01:02,755 --> 01:01:07,256
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what made it real rough for me and then sort of discouraged me a little bit.

1029
01:01:07,336 --> 01:01:12,378
