[SPEAKER_00]: Mr. Terry would call me every day.

1038
01:01:57,049 --> 01:02:02,112
[SPEAKER_00]: He didn't care too much about winning, is what he said, but he wanted to worry about developing players.

1039
01:02:02,732 --> 01:02:16,999
[SPEAKER_00]: And I had three or four pitchers that looked real good, Huey East, Reuben Fisher, Lou Henshaw that used to be with the Cubs, Roy Henshaw, and one or two of them went up and relieved for a boy by the name of Huey East.

1040
01:02:17,572 --> 01:02:18,352
[SPEAKER_00]: real good pitcher.

1041
01:02:18,953 --> 01:02:27,556
[SPEAKER_00]: Sid Gordon was a shortstop at the time that I tried to play with him to make him a shortstop and eventually I had to tell Terry that I didn't think he could make it.

